  "family": {
    "id": "55c3e433-integrated-adoption",
    "issue": "3ee00fcf",
    "purpose": "decoder-family",
    "description": "Confirmation of the delivered QC route against pinned pre-change production, under the adoption-family contract of dev/active/55c3e433-aff3ct-ldpc-gaps/plan.md. The baseline arm gf2-batch-pre-change is the tuned production arm built from the tree immediately before the QC decoder core merged, under the committed coding envelope. The candidate arm gf2-batch-qc-candidate is the tuned production arm built from the tree carrying the QC decoder and its route, under the candidate envelope experiments/aff3ct-ldpc-gaps/tuning-profiles/qc-route-candidate.json, with NR BG1 Z=384 structure attached after an exact parity-check comparison outside timing. The candidate carries no check variant. Both arms decode by default construction under their installed envelope. The QC route's selection predicate of qc-go-rule takes NR BG1 Z=384 at one worker with one frame and at twelve workers with eight frames per worker, the cells with objective improvement; every other cell keeps its existing route and has objective non-regression. The AList graphs, recorded LLRs, f32 flooding NMS factor 0.75, cap 50, syndrome stopping, timed prefix and steady-state decode boundary are those of 55c3e433-nr-route-pilot and 55c3e433-check-variants. Each worker owns its decoder before timing; conversion, dispatch and information-window extraction are included. Stages are one twelve-pair pilot, a freeze by experiments/aff3ct-ldpc-gaps/freeze-confirmation.py with resolution from that pilot, and one 24-pair confirmation of the six cells. This family's ledger starts empty; the earlier families of @/issue/55c3e433 asked other questions on their own ledgers, and no estimate here reuses them. Project-level final integration stays with the 1362381c scorecard, so the family declares no holdout."
  },
  "frozen": {
    "frozen_utc": "2026-11-03T20:49:03Z"
  },
  "effect": {
    "worthwhile_speedup": 1.25,
    "rationale": "FI-3's material-gap threshold, which reflects the QC delivery's size of an estimated 600 to 1,200 lines; a smaller repeatable gain on the targeted cells does not repay that maintenance (qc-go-rule).",
    "measurement_resolution": null,
    "resolution_evidence": null,
    "equivalence_margin": 1.1,
    "equivalence_rationale": "A cell the selection predicate keeps on its existing route may lose at most ten percent before the route counts as a regression there; the margin is the epic's equivalence margin, fixed before this pilot, and the canonical freezer stops when pilot resolution reaches it and never widens it from results.",
    "material_gap_threshold": null,
    "material_gap_rationale": "The adoption family pairs two gf2 builds; it has no comparator-gap cells."
  },
